caption:
Ottawa families, we’re so excited to continue exploring all the outdoor (and some indoor) activities that the city has to offer this spring and summer! Last year we had a new walker and this year, we’ll have a full blown toddler to explore with. While we primarily spend time in the west/south end of the city, I’m sure we will be visiting some other spots too. Follow along to see what we get up to, and share your favourite spots! 
-
Some of our favourite spots from last year:
@millersfarmandmarket 
@valleyviewlittleanimalfarm 
@thelogfarm 
@metcalfefarmersmarket and @greelygoodmarket with their kids play areas
The fairs in the south (stay tuned for more info)
#ottawaevents #ottawafamily #ottawamom #ottawakids #ottawaliving

Ottawa, @workshoptrunksale is back for their Legendary spring trunk sale in collaboration with @nextdoorottawa and @vpop613 ♥️ Every year, I get so excited for the spring and fall trunk sales. They feature all Canadian designers and pieces up to 70% off! And, I always leave with a few staple pieces (like these brown pants I picked up 3 years ago). 
-
The trunk sale runs
 April 9 through 10am - 8pm
April 10 10am-7pm
April 11 - 12 11am-5pm (and @vpop613 vintage and thrift vendors join over the weekend) 
📍955A Gladstone + parking on site 
A great opportunity to support Canadian, local and discover vintage/thrifted finds! You never know what you’ll find but I can promise you it will be a blast! 
-
A breakdown of the trunk sale pieces featured in this video:
@lights.of.all Astoria dress size M $165 (linen)
@lights.of.all Prius dress size M $90
@melow_par_melissa_bolduc Kim dress size S $143
@advikaclothing cropped tank size L $44.5
@kazakmtl Verona skirt size M $88.8
@tangenteclothing Heidi pants size M $70
I’ve got tons more to share in stories throughout the sale, so stay tuned! They have so many styles, prints and silhouettes. Check it out for some staple pieces. 
P.s. my outfit is also all Canadian (@figclothing pants and @rightfulowner top) 
#ottawaevents #ottawamom #ottawasmallbusiness #canadiansmallbusiness #canadianmade 🇨🇦

Save the date for @fetchlocalmarkets first market of the season on May 9th 10AM - 3PM at the Place D’Orleans Park and Ride (subsequent markets are at Ray Friel Rec). They sent over a box of goodies from some of the vendors that will be at the market and there’s so many goodies in here. I love that this box is curated for me because it’s actually perfect! ♥️ I can’t wait to check out the market this season and discover new to me vendors! It’s the perfect way to support local. In my box:
